---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LoopMark from "../components/LoopMark.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Datafore is a clinic intelligence company based in Burnaby, BC, building the layer between what clinic data shows and what actually gets done."
>
  <section class="border-b border-graphite-200 bg-bone">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-graphite-950 md:text-5xl">About Datafore</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
        Datafore began as a data and analytics consultancy, helping organisations get value out of data they
        already had. Doing that work repeatedly made one gap obvious: the reporting was rarely the hard part.
        Getting anything to happen as a result was.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-graphite-950">Why allied health</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
          Private clinics — physiotherapy, chiropractic, massage therapy, mental health — sit on years of detailed
          operational data and get almost no strategic use out of it. Their software was built to run the day, not
          to answer how the business is doing. Owners end up reconstructing the picture by hand, if at all, while a
          meaningful share of revenue leaves through no-shows, gaps and quiet patient churn.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
          It's a gap that shows up in every clinic we talk to, and it's specific enough to solve properly rather
          than generically.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-graphite-950">How we think about it</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
          Practitioners already run a disciplined loop: assess, treat, reassess. Nobody would accept a course of
          treatment that skipped the reassessment. Yet that's exactly how clinic reporting usually works — a number
          is produced, and nothing follows from it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
          Datafore applies the clinical method to the clinic itself. That's the whole idea, and everything in the
          product is downstream of it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-graphite-200 bg-bone-dim">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
      <p class="measure-label text-vital-700">Team</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-6 rounded-lg border border-graphite-200 bg-white p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
        <img src={withBase("/images/sandeep-mehra.jpg")} alt="Sandeep Mehra" class="h-28 w-28 rounded-full object-cover" />
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-graphite-950">Sandeep Mehra</h3>
            <LoopMark size={24} active={3} class="text-vital-600" />
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-vital-700">Product Manager, Analytics</p>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/smehra2/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-graphite-600 underline decoration-graphite-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-vital-700"
          >
            Connect on LinkedIn
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-graphite-600">
        We're based in Burnaby, BC, and small by design at this stage — building alongside founding clinics across
        the province before going wider. If that's the kind of problem you want to work on, get in touch.
      </p>
      <a
        href={withBase("/contact/")}
        class="mt-6 inline-block rounded bg-vital-600 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-vital-700"
      >
        Get in touch
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
